From 8ea31f74c592e81e3a87baefed5346483c099cac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "sh.chao" <sh.chao@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 15:02:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] r25-1-0090: cull compact command bounds before replay

Extend the existing 32x32 holder-space index with one conservative 8-byte
quantized bound per command. The bound is produced from the same PDFium page
object rectangle already read while building the index, so compilation gains
no second object scan. During tile replay, the ordered candidate cursor rejects
coarse-bin false positives before live object lookup while preserving command
order and all existing raster/composite behavior.

Quantization rounds outward, invalid or unsupported bounds become full-holder
bounds, structural mismatches abandon the index, and full-page queries disable
the compact filter. Retained bounds memory is capped at 32 MiB. Remove the now
redundant live rectangle test and report boundsRejected/compactBoundsBytes so
device logs can distinguish index precision wins from genuinely dense tiles.

